From bd4c214b0a7450e2a521f6534cce3b001676988b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 21:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore(migrations): renumber feature migrations to 0150..0156

Upstream released 0149_channel_live_pinned_index, and this branch already used
0149 for collectible usernames. Two files claiming one version is not a git
conflict -- both simply coexist -- but iofs.New then fails with "duplicate
migration file", so MigrateAndStatus errors and the server refuses to start.

Version numbers are ordering, not identity, so the branch yields 0149 to upstream
and shifts its own chain up by one:

  0149 collectible_usernames        -> 0150
  0150 account_rating               -> 0151
  0151 collectible_username_reissue -> 0152
  0152 verify_service_bot           -> 0153
  0153 verification_applications    -> 0154
  0154 bot_verification             -> 0155
  0155 verifier_service_bot         -> 0156

Renumbering is safe here only because none of these migrations has been applied
to a production database yet: a deployment that already recorded version 149 for
collectible_usernames would need its schema_migrations row corrected by hand
instead. Comments, docs and the schema-version assertion move with the numbers.
